<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">OECD</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1961">1961</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) is an intergovernmental organisation of mostly high-income democracies, founded in 1961 as the successor to the body that administered Marshall Plan aid. Based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, it gathers economic statistics, compares policies and sets standards on matters such as taxation and education. Chile, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> and Israel joined in 2010 and Latvia in 2016.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oecd.jpg" alt="OECD" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MySociety · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ch%C3%A2teau_de_la_Muette,_Paris_20_March_2019_004.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…227 diplomatic missions and relations with more than 190 countries, belongs to the Council of Europe, NATO, the <b>OECD</b>, the G7, the G20, the World Bank and the IMF, has kept a strong alliance with France and all its neighbours since 1990 and is widely considered a great…</blockquote><a href="/empire/federal-republic-of-germany">Federal Republic of Germany · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…accession to the European Communities in 1979, completed entry to the single market in 1982, joined the Economic and Monetary Union in June 2000 and adopted the euro in January 2001, and is a founding member of the <b>OECD</b>, the Black Sea Economic Cooperation and the United Nations.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hellenic-republic">Hellenic Republic · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Hungary nevertheless became an <b>OECD</b> high-income mixed economy, more than 80% privately owned, with a skilled workforce and one of the lowest levels of income inequality in the world.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hungary">Hungary · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>OECD</b> named it an uncooperative jurisdiction in 2004 and moved it to the white list in 2009 after twelve information-exchange treaties; in June 2024 the Financial Action Task Force placed Monaco on its grey list.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-monaco">Principality of Monaco · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>It joined the United Nations in 1955, is a founding member of the <b>OECD</b> and Interpol, and hosts the Organization for Security and Co-operation in Europe and the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-austria">Republic of Austria · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Chile grew rapidly, joined the <b>OECD</b> in 2010 and cut poverty sharply, but inequality and the cost of services fuelled mass protests in October 2019, the estallido social.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Republic of Chile · Into the Present</a></li></ul></section>
